# Justified exceptions for scripts/guards/no-integration-names.sh.
# Format: path_regex:line_regex   (split at the first colon; both are ERE, matched
# against the file path and the matched line respectively).
# Keep entries narrow. Each needs a reason comment above it.

# LLM provider hosts are allowed by design (known_llm_hosts in aurora-llm/aurora-config).
# (no entries yet; add e.g.)
# ^crates/aurora-llm/.*:known_llm_hosts

# (P4-GSL) A sample `Link` header in a unit test of the host-neutral pagination parser.
^crates/aurora-registry/src/library\.rs$:gitlab\.example

# (FIX-123, D-215) The table of built-in apps that became connect methods of another app: an upgrade
# shim that moves the connections of installs still holding the old apps. It is the one place the
# core names built-in packages, and it is data, not integration behaviour.
^crates/aurora-registry/src/superseded\.rs$:.*

# (P5-ASRC, D-250) The addon-source URL normaliser turns a git forge's repository page URL into the
# raw URL of its manifest (`github.com/o/r` → `raw.githubusercontent.com/…`, a `gitlab.` host →
# `…/-/raw/HEAD/…`): URL shaping the admin's paste needs, not integration behaviour, and it names
# no product beyond the two raw-file URL layouts.
^services/aurora-api/src/domains/addon_sources/manifest\.rs$:([Gg]it[Hh]ub|[Gg]it[Ll]ab)

# (P5-SKLIB-1, D-448, C-1123) The git address parser's unit table: sample addresses of the forges whose page
# URLs people paste (`/tree/`, `/-/tree/`, `/blob/` shapes). The parser is host-neutral (the page-URL shapes are
# the only thing it knows), and the names appear only in the test table.
^crates/aurora-core/src/git_url\.rs$:([Gg]it[Hh]ub|[Gg]it[Ll]ab|[Bb]it[Bb]ucket)

# (P5-SKLIB-1, D-448, C-1127) The one-off backfill that gives the libraries of the two retired GitHub/GitLab
# app connections their clone address (a migration, never run again; data, not integration behaviour).
^crates/aurora-db/migrations/20261201000270_skill_library_git_url\.sql$:([Gg]it[Hh]ub|[Gg]it[Ll]ab|github\.com|gitlab\.com)

# (FIX-142) Comments in the Markdown sanitizer and its tests that cite the dialect measurements the
# D-227/D-270 exceptions rest on (the pinned chat server's parser behaviour). Comments only: no code
# in core names the product.
^crates/aurora-core/src/sanitize/safe(/tests)?\.rs$:^[[:space:]]*///?.*Mattermost

# Bundled top-10k common-password list (I-11) is data, not integration code.
^services/aurora-api/data/common-passwords\.txt$:.*

# (P4-PRV-1) The previews-domain validator's coarse public-suffix list: `github.io` is a
# public suffix that must never be a previews domain (no real integration code).
^crates/aurora-config/src/validate\.rs$:github\.io

# (P6-TPL-1, C-1141) The template crate's unit-test fixtures, gathered in one file: they name the
# same apps and library hosts C-1141's own examples use (Jira project inputs, atlassian/microsoft-365/
# caldav `any_of` groups, GitHub release-URL and gitlab.cern.ch library addresses). The crate parses
# template data; the names appear only in test fixtures, never in shipped behaviour.
^crates/aurora-template/src/test_fixtures\.rs$:([Jj]ira|[Aa]tlassian|[Mm]icrosoft|[Cc]al[Dd][Aa][Vv]|[Gg]it[Hh]ub|[Gg]it[Ll]ab)

# (PART 0, fix-241-243 lane) The repository-metadata rule: a `.github` folder is a repository's own
# metadata, never package, template or library content. The only forge name the core knows is the
# path predicate and the folder literal it matches: `has_github_segment` (and its `a_github_folder`
# tests), `.github` in the predicate, its callers and their comments, and the plugin packer, which
# skips such paths when collecting skill files. No integration behaviour.
^(crates/aurora-core/src/meta_paths|crates/aurora-registry/src/package|crates/aurora-template/src/archive|crates/aurora-template/src/validate|(crates|services)/aurora-cli/src/template|services/aurora-cli/src/plugin/pack|services/aurora-api/src/domains/agent_templates/check|services/aurora-api/src/domains/skill_libraries/content|services/aurora-api/src/domains/skill_libraries/git/mod)\.rs$:[._]github
